RESULT
============================================================================================
  The lowest Cassini-safe exponent is n = 3, which forces
  kappa = 1/3 = 0.333   against the measured
  0.529 +- 0.034 (README)  --  off by 5.8 sigma.
  The RAR-preferred n = 3 gives kappa = 1/3 = 0.333
      but its Q_zz is 0.61x the Cassini ceiling.

READING: inside a single mu_n kernel there is a FORK, not a gap.
  Family (A) BN11  : n and kappa are DECOUPLED -> Cassini satisfiable,
                     but then nothing connects a_0 to Lambda.
  Family (B) Mandel: n IS kappa -> you may have the relation OR Cassini.
  You cannot have both with one exponent.

CAVEATS: (i) SPARC-only rms on committed binned points, no per-galaxy
         nuisance (Upsilon_disk) fit -- route1B flags that as undecided;
         (ii) family (A) is given a_0 = A0C fixed, which is its free dial;
         (iii) the DHF24 quadrature is this lane's reconstruction of
         route1B's committed pipeline, not an independent derivation.

